\section*{Problem}
Heather's razors come 4 to a pack and cost \$4.00 a pack. They are currently on sale for buy one get one free. She also has a \$2.00 coupon. How much will each individual razor cost, in cents, after the discount if she buys 2 packs of razors?

\section*{Solution}
If she buys 2 packs of razors, she will get 8 razors for free because 2 x 4 = 8. Since she has a coupon for \$2.00, she will pay \$6.00 for 2 packs of razors because 8 - 2 = 6. If she buys 2 packs of razors for \$6.00, that means each razor costs \$0.75 because 6 / 8 = 0.75. If each razor costs \$0.75, that means each razor costs 75 cents because 100 x 0.75 = 75. Therefore, the answer is \boxed{75}.

